\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Reflecting the value of a field}
\date{2026-11-26}

\p{The [site reflection](fdip-007M) sends a field value at
#{(y,u)} to the site #{(y,-u)}. A forward step in time then
goes backward. In a centered difference this exchanges the two
neighboring values. A spin field also has a direction operator
multiplying that difference. How can reflection act on the
spin value so that the time term is carried to the reflected
field operator? What becomes of the link between two such
neighboring values?}
